  "freshIndependentAnswers": [
    {
      "qid": 13,
      "independentAnswer": "146",
      "reasoning": "Let k=(2log_2 n+1)/3. Since k is a natural number at most 6, k∈{1,2,3,4,5,6}, and log_2 n=(3k−1)/2. For n to be a natural number, this exponent must be an integer, so k is odd: k=1,3,5. The corresponding n are 2,16,128, whose sum is 146. Thus choice ③.",
      "answerCardinality": 1
    },
    {
      "qid": 23,
      "independentAnswer": "2",
      "reasoning": "Write B=(b,log_3 b). Since A and B lie on a line of slope −1, x+y has the same value at both. The function h(x)=x+3^x is strictly increasing; reflecting B across y=x gives (log_3 b,b), also on y=3^x and with the same coordinate sum, so A=(log_3 b,b). Put t=log_3 b>0. Then AB=√2(b−t)=24√2, hence b−t=24 and the vertical height from A to horizontal BC is 24. The area 312 gives BC=2·312/24=26. As C=(log_3 t,t), b−log_3 t=26; subtract b−t=24 to get t−log_3 t=2. Since b=3^t and b−t=24, t satisfies 3^t−t=24. For t>0 this function is strictly increasing (derivative ln(3)·3^t−1>0), so its unique solution is t=3. Then b=27 and log_3 t=1. Finally α=x_A=t=3, so α−log_3 α=3−1=2.",
      "answerCardinality": 1
    }
  ],
